{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\sqrt{1+8t}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((3+2t)^{3/2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(1+8t)^{-1/2}\\cdot 8,\\frac{3}{2}(3+2t)^{1/2}\\cdot 2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{1+8t}},3\\sqrt{3+2t}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=3,$ we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =⟨\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{1+8(3)}},3\\sqrt{3+2(3)}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{25}},3\\sqrt{9}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{20}{5},3(3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,9⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333506 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333507 13194139535142 true] [17592186333506 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333508 13194139535142 true] [17592186333506 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535142 true] [17592186333506 1041 "field-1" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333506 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333508 13194139535142 true] [17592186333506 1110 #uuid "16d9c637-816b-5e0f-aadd-9066f3e555aa" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333507 1034 "25" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333507 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535142 true] [17592186333507 1111 #uuid "7edc0ef2-3374-5396-bf68-fe6d96efaf91" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333508 1034 "4" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333508 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535142 true] [17592186333508 1111 #uuid "8c132b5e-7bda-554f-bc5b-a5c02cc0c708" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333509 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333510 13194139535142 true] [17592186333509 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535142 true] [17592186333509 1041 "field-2" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333509 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333510 13194139535142 true] [17592186333509 1110 #uuid "bce0b200-17e2-503f-95eb-67ac0ce7ad5b" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333510 1034 "9" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333510 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535142 true] [17592186333510 1111 #uuid "6c292866-73c9-5d3b-a563-fa23a15c6a9d" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333511 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333512 13194139535142 true] [17592186333511 1089 "q-352572" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333511 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535142 true] [17592186333511 1100 "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\frac{5{t}^{2}}{2},\\,3t+2⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed  $|v|$ of the particle at time $t=3.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe speed at time $t=3$ is\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535142 true] [17592186333511 1113 #uuid "810e6c21-1003-5a47-b790-30b10392715b" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333511 1145 "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{5{t}^{2}}{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t+2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5t,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=3,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =⟨5(3),\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨15,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=3$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(3),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(3)| & =\\sqrt{{15}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{225+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{234} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{26}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333512 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333513 13194139535142 true] [17592186333512 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535142 true] [17592186333512 1041 "field-1" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333512 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333513 13194139535142 true] [17592186333512 1110 #uuid "4e8ceebc-1b05-539e-91d2-8fbd23848387" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333513 1034 "3\\sqrt{26}" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333513 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535142 true] [17592186333513 1111 #uuid "4d5835d4-8696-554f-bb70-a2bda4ac2d94" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333514 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333515 13194139535142 true] [17592186333514 1089 "q-352584" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333514 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535142 true] [17592186333514 1100 "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+2),\\,\\frac{4}{t}⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed $|v|$ of the particle at time $t=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe speed at time $t=2$ is\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535142 true] [17592186333514 1113 #uuid "b661ab3f-53c8-53bd-9aca-1b6a65f8f496" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333514 1145 "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+2)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{4}{t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{t+2},\\,-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=2,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =⟨\\frac{1}{2+2},\\,-\\frac{4}{{2}^{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{4},\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=2$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(2),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(2)| & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}+{(-1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{16}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333515 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333516 13194139535142 true] [17592186333515 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535142 true] [17592186333515 1041 "field-1" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333515 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333516 13194139535142 true] [17592186333515 1110 #uuid "ec00e37a-ad51-598d-b18a-2ef6678ae717" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333516 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{4}" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333516 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535142 true] [17592186333516 1111 #uuid "fc38d2dc-1527-56e3-96af-51823830504a" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333517 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333518 13194139535142 true] [17592186333517 1089 "q-352588" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333517 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535142 true] [17592186333517 1100 "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+3),\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed $|v|$ of the particle at time $t=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe speed at time $t=1$ is\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535142 true] [17592186333517 1113 #uuid "edb7fca2-61e2-5800-a4c9-2d1de8e94995" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333517 1145 "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+3)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{t+3},\\,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=1,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =⟨\\frac{1}{1+3},\\,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{4},\\,\\frac{1}{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=1$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(1),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(1)| & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{16}+\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333518 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333519 13194139535142 true] [17592186333518 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535142 true] [17592186333518 1041 "field-1" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333518 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333519 13194139535142 true] [17592186333518 1110 #uuid "42b67214-0fe8-5675-94ac-cef6f791a1f7" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333519 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333519 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535142 true] [17592186333519 1111 #uuid "d720b213-48a4-514d-bb6a-de868f54160f" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333520 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333521 13194139535142 true] [17592186333520 1089 "q-352596" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333520 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535142 true] [17592186333520 1100 "A particle $P$ is moving in the $x$-$y$ plane. Its position vector relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}t),\\,\\sqrt{t+2}⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle at time $t=2.$\n\nThe speed at time $t=2$ is\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535142 true] [17592186333520 1113 #uuid "def01361-ad83-523b-8ea1-25745a466c56" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333520 1145 "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}t)),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t+2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}t),\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t+2}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=2,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =⟨-2\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ),\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2+2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\frac{1}{4}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=2$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(2),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(2)| & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333521 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333522 13194139535142 true] [17592186333521 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333523 13194139535142 true] [17592186333521 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535142 true] [17592186333521 1041 "field-1" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333521 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333523 13194139535142 true] [17592186333521 1110 #uuid "7f449c06-653a-5e84-804c-c7eb77aa2bd9" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333522 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535142 true] [17592186333522 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535142 true] [1759218633